      <div type="clause" n="5.2d">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 5.2d</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.2d" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="286" ed="#liebermann"/>And na<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_5-2d.lnote.oe.13"/> þearf ænig mynstermunuc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ICn_5-2d.lnote.oe.14"/> ahwær mid rihte fæhðbote biddan ne fæhþbote betan; he gæð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_5-2d.lnote.oe.15"/> of his mægðlage, þonne he gebyhð to regollage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.2d" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="286" ed="#liebermann"/>And ne þærf ænig mynstermunuc áhwer mid rihte fæhþbóte biddan ne fæhþbote betan: he gað of his mægðlage, þonne he gebyhþ to regollage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.2d" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="286" ed="#liebermann"/>Monachus ęcclesiasticus non debet aliquam de homine occiso persolutionem exigere uel emendare, quia cognationis suę legem exiit, cum se regularis conuersationis disciplinę mancipauit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.2d" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="287" ed="#liebermann"/>Nullus monachus monasterialis debet emendare homicidium nec petere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ICn_5-2d.lnote.oe.14-2"/> emendationem homicidii, licet sit parens occisoris<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_5-2d.lnote.oe.1"/> (occidentium) uel occisi, quia ubi intrat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_5-2d.lnote.oe.15-2"/> monasterium pro tenenda regula, relinquit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_5-2d.lnote.oe.16"/> ea quę sunt secularia . . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_5-2d.lnote.oe.17"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.2d" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="287" ed="#liebermann"/>Neque debet monasterii monacus satisfaccionem cause mortis humane uel soluere uel deprecari, quoniam ipse egreditur de lege cognacionis, cum regule legem subit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="5a.2d" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="160" ed="#robertson"/>And na þearf ænig mynstermunuc ahwær mid rihte fæhðbote biddan ne fæhþbote betan; he gæð of his mægðlage, þonne he gebyhð to regollage.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="238" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And na þearf ænig mynstermunuc ahwær mid rihte fæhðbote biddan ne fæhþbote betan; he gæð of his mægðlage þonne he gebyhð to regollage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="287" ed="#liebermann"/>Und nicht darf ein Klostermönch irgendwo gesetzlich Geldbusse für Todtschlag [verübt an seinem Verwandten] fordern, noch auch Geldbusse für Todtschlag [verübt durch seinen Verwandten] zahlen: er tritt aus seinem Sippenrecht, sobald er sich dem Rechte der Ordensregel unterwirft.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And no monk of a minster may anywhere lawfully demand feud-compensation [for the killing of his kinsman] or pay feud-compensation [for a killing by his kinsman]: he leaves his kin-law when he submits to the law of the rule.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="161" ed="#robertson"/>And no monk who belongs to a monastery anywhere may lawfully either demand or pay any compensation incurred by vendetta. He leaves the law of his kindred behind when he accepts monastic rule.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="239" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And no monk anywhere who belongs to a monastery is permitted to either claim or pay compensation related to a feud; he renounces the rights of his kindred when he accepts the monastic rule.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="287"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_25">VIII Atr 25</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 25</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_25">VIII Atr 25–27.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 5:2d-5:4: VIII Atr 25-27:1</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VIII Atr 25.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 287, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
